00:14:34,105 --> 00:14:34,768
Bird!

269
00:14:39,346 --> 00:14:41,973
You should spend a day at the beach.
Get some sun.

270
00:14:43,209 --> 00:14:44,060
Right, so...

271
00:14:44,209 --> 00:14:44,997
Marketing...

272
00:14:45,202 --> 00:14:46,582
thought we could offset

273
00:14:46,606 --> 00:14:47,895
some of the costs by...

274
00:14:47,920 --> 00:14:49,568
Enough about cost.

275
00:14:50,228 --> 00:14:52,430
John Hammond entrusted me
with his dying wish,

276
00:14:52,455 --> 00:14:54,617
and not once did he mention profits.

277
00:14:54,642 --> 00:14:56,217
Spare no expense,

278
00:14:56,241 --> 00:14:58,219
he used to say.
I appreciate that but...

279
00:14:58,258 --> 00:15:01,132
the reality of operating
a theme park requires...

280
00:15:01,157 --> 00:15:03,159
Don't forget why we built this place, Claire.

281
00:15:03,493 --> 00:15:07,091
Jurassic World exists to remind us
how very small we are.

282
00:15:07,116 --> 00:15:09,844
How new. You can't put a price on that.

283
00:15:09,960 --> 00:15:10,940
Now please...

284
00:15:11,649 --> 00:15:12,849
we are flying.

285
00:15:14,520 --> 00:15:15,839
Breathe.

286
00:15:43,913 --> 00:15:44,765
Is he ok?

287
00:15:45,106 --> 00:15:47,220
Are you ok?
He is just being dramatic.

288
00:15:48,146 --> 00:15:49,266
Are you still building?

289
00:15:50,680 --> 00:15:52,651
We planned to open in May,

290
00:15:52,676 --> 00:15:54,608
but Asset Containment insisted

291
00:15:54,632 --> 00:15:56,255
we build the walls up higher.

292
00:15:56,707 --> 00:15:58,227
It's bigger than expected.

293
00:16:04,493 --> 00:16:05,520
It's a good sign.

294
00:16:07,840 --> 00:16:10,684
We hit a few speed bumps early on.

295
00:16:10,940 --> 00:16:13,700
It began to anticipate
where the food would come from.

296
00:16:14,153 --> 00:16:16,273
One of the handlers nearly lost an arm.

297
00:16:16,312 --> 00:16:17,923
The others threatened to quit,

298
00:16:17,947 --> 00:16:19,759
if I could not guarantee their safety.

299
00:16:20,620 --> 00:16:22,026
She is intelligent then?

300
00:16:22,860 --> 00:16:24,133
For a dinosaur.

301
00:16:24,873 --> 00:16:26,013
And that?

302
00:16:31,373 --> 00:16:32,977
It tried to break the glass.

303
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:35,526
I like her spirit.

304
00:16:57,280 --> 00:16:58,339
It's white.

305
00:16:59,301 --> 00:17:00,775
You never told me it was white.

306
00:17:06,540 --> 00:17:07,960
Think it will scare the kids?

307
00:17:09,600 --> 00:17:10,613
The kids?

308
00:17:12,240 --> 00:17:14,100
This will give the parents nightmares.

309
00:17:15,880 --> 00:17:17,484
Is that good?

310
00:17:19,400 --> 00:17:21,233
It's fantastic.

311
00:17:25,746 --> 00:17:26,746
Can she see us?

312
00:17:28,080 --> 00:17:30,208
They say it can sense thermal radiation.

313
00:17:30,280 --> 00:17:31,340
Like snakes.

314
00:17:32,493 --> 00:17:34,020
I thought there were two of them.

315
00:17:34,800 --> 00:17:38,247
There was a sibling in case
this one didn't survive infancy.

316
00:17:38,413 --> 00:17:39,547
Where is the sibling?

317
00:17:40,440 --> 00:17:41,487
She ate it.

318
00:17:49,777 --> 00:17:50,724
So,

319
00:17:50,837 --> 00:17:52,830
the paddock is quite safe, then?

320
00:17:53,576 --> 00:17:55,229
We have the best...

321
00:17:55,403 --> 00:17:57,243
structural engineers in the world.

322
00:17:58,279 --> 00:17:59,476
Yeah, so did Hammond.

323
00:18:02,066 --> 00:18:04,327
There is an American Navy man here.

324
00:18:04,352 --> 00:18:07,153
Part of a research program
one of my companies is running.

325
00:18:07,480 --> 00:18:08,680
Owen Grady.

326
00:18:10,334 --> 00:18:11,401
I know who he is.

327
00:18:11,520 --> 00:18:13,443
His animals often try to escape.

328
00:18:13,520 --> 00:18:14,540
They are smart.

329
00:18:15,281 --> 00:18:16,594
He has to be smarter.

330
00:18:16,833 --> 00:18:18,352
He only thinks he is smarter.

331
00:18:19,926 --> 00:18:21,952
I want you to bring him in.

332
00:18:22,600 --> 00:18:23,965
Let him inspect the paddock.

333
00:18:25,913 --> 00:18:27,800
Maybe he sees something we can't.

334
00:18:44,640 --> 00:18:45,493
Hold!

335
00:18:52,960 --> 00:18:53,544
Hey!

336
00:18:58,720 --> 00:18:59,391
Ok!

337
00:19:00,720 --> 00:19:01,881
Eyes on me.

338
00:19:02,520 --> 00:19:03,300
Blue?

339
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:04,786
Blue!

340
00:19:05,960 --> 00:19:06,746
Watch it.

341
00:19:07,733 --> 00:19:08,734
Charlie. Hey!

342
00:19:09,160 --> 00:19:10,500
Don't give me that shit!

343
00:19:11,440 --> 00:19:12,233
Delta!

344
00:19:12,640 --> 00:19:13,540
Lock it up!

345
00:19:15,186 --> 00:19:16,126
Good!

346
00:19:16,833 --> 00:19:17,686
And...

347
00:19:18,243 --> 00:19:19,153
we are moving!

348
00:19:25,873 --> 00:19:26,873
Hold!

349
00:19:28,553 --> 00:19:29,365
That's good.

350
00:19:29,868 --> 00:19:31,446
That is damn good.

351
00:19:33,067 --> 00:19:34,114
Very good!

352
00:19:34,139 --> 00:19:35,329
See Charlie,

353
00:19:35,353 --> 00:19:36,506
that's what you get!

354
00:19:37,080 --> 00:19:39,242
Echo, there you go!
Delta!

355
00:19:41,580 --> 00:19:42,320
Blue?

356
00:19:45,633 --> 00:19:46,693
This one is for you.

357
00:19:50,519 --> 00:19:51,415
Hold!

358
00:19:52,866 --> 00:19:53,913
Eyes up!

359
00:19:57,346 --> 00:19:58,058
Go.

360
00:20:05,416 --> 00:20:06,727
You finally did it man.

361
00:20:06,972 --> 00:20:07,809
Owen.

362
00:20:10,985 --> 00:20:12,908
I was starting to think
I hired the wrong guys,

363
00:20:12,933 --> 00:20:14,740
but damn, you got them
eating out of your palm.

364
00:20:14,991 --> 00:20:17,255
You came on a good day.
It's not usually a happy ending.

365
00:20:17,280 --> 00:20:18,911
Is that why you are not
sending in your reports?

366
00:20:19,234 --> 00:20:20,458
We have been busy.

367
00:20:20,646 --> 00:20:22,438
Not too busy to cash your paychecks.

368
00:20:23,920 --> 00:20:25,105
What do you need, buddy?

369
00:20:26,226 --> 00:20:27,146
A field test.

370
00:20:28,146 --> 00:20:28,799
Hey.

371
00:20:29,253 --> 00:20:31,666
I have just seen they can
respond to commands.

372
00:20:31,806 --> 00:20:34,161
We need to take the research
and get it on its feet.

373
00:20:34,186 --> 00:20:35,365
These are wild animals, Hoskins.

374
00:20:35,390 --> 00:20:37,166
Trust me, you don't want them in the field.

375
00:20:37,506 --> 00:20:39,101
I just saw a bond.

376
00:20:39,252 --> 00:20:40,379
A real bond.

377
00:20:40,419 --> 00:20:42,159
Between man and beast.

378
00:20:42,766 --> 00:20:44,440
You are in my way.
Come on.

379
00:20:44,819 --> 00:20:46,752
We are the same.
We are dogs of war.

380
00:20:47,065 --> 00:20:49,899
We know that the military
needs to reduce casualties.

381
00:20:50,133 --> 00:20:52,135
Some people think that
robots are the future.

382
00:20:52,160 --> 00:20:54,731
Look, nature gave us the most effective

383
00:20:54,800 --> 00:20:57,546
killing machines 75 million years ago.

384
00:20:57,746 --> 00:20:59,773
And now we know they can take orders.

385
00:21:00,246 --> 00:21:02,629
We finally make progress
and that's the first thing he says?

386
00:21:02,922 --> 00:21:04,195
Make a weapon?

387
00:21:04,413 --> 00:21:05,275
Shit.

388
00:21:05,906 --> 00:21:07,271
Come on, gents.

389
00:21:07,642 --> 00:21:09,142
It's grown-up time.

390
00:21:09,560 --> 00:21:11,842
Drones can't search tunnels and caves.

391
00:21:11,920 --> 00:21:13,215
And they are hackable.

392
00:21:13,240 --> 00:21:15,048
The minute a real war breaks out,

393
00:21:15,073 --> 00:21:16,853
all that fancy tech is gonna go dark.

394
00:21:17,147 --> 00:21:19,640
But that tech is not gonna eat them
if they forget to feed it.

395
00:21:20,720 --> 00:21:22,529
Look, look at these creatures.

396
00:21:22,726 --> 00:21:25,701
They have got millions
of years of instinct in their cells,

397
00:21:25,726 --> 00:21:27,019
instinct that we can program.

398
00:21:27,880 --> 00:21:30,026
Their loyalty cannot be bought.

399
00:21:31,177 --> 00:21:32,508
These guys are gonna run

400
00:21:32,533 --> 00:21:34,683
straight into the enemy's teeth
and eat them,

401
00:21:34,708 --> 00:21:36,001
belt buckle and all.

402
00:21:36,653 --> 00:21:38,868
What if they decide,
they wanna be in control?

403
00:21:39,640 --> 00:21:41,940
Well, then we remind them who is.
We terminate the rogues.

404
00:21:42,546 --> 00:21:44,053
Promote only loyal bloodlines.

405
00:21:45,800 --> 00:21:46,293
What?

406
00:21:46,890 --> 00:21:47,913
What's so funny?

407
00:21:51,400 --> 00:21:52,741
I don't know.
You come here

408
00:21:52,766 --> 00:21:54,260
and you don't learn
anything about these animals

409
00:21:54,285 --> 00:21:55,753
except what you want to know.

410
00:21:57,080 --> 00:21:59,139
You made them
and now you think you own them.

411
00:21:59,786 --> 00:22:01,053
We do own them.

412
00:22:02,486 --> 00:22:04,026
Extinct animals have no rights.

413
00:22:05,000 --> 00:22:06,605
They are not extinct anymore, Hoskins.

414
00:22:06,630 --> 00:22:07,513
Exactly.

415
00:22:08,108 --> 00:22:09,612
We are sitting on a goldmine.

416
00:22:09,928 --> 00:22:13,448
And Masrani is using it
to stock a petting zoo.

417
00:22:13,541 --> 00:22:15,246
He just wants to teach people
some humility.

418
00:22:15,271 --> 00:22:16,327
He doesn't make weapons.

419
00:22:16,352 --> 00:22:19,089
You think that the eighth
richest man in the world

420
00:22:19,114 --> 00:22:20,577
is only into oil,

421
00:22:20,774 --> 00:22:21,662
telecom,

422
00:22:21,707 --> 00:22:23,194
and family fun parks?

423
00:22:23,520 --> 00:22:25,453
He is so diversified,
he doesn't even know what he owns.

424
00:22:25,478 --> 00:22:27,613
How long has InGen
been practicing this pitch?

425
00:22:27,873 --> 00:22:30,160
Since the day
we hired you out of the Navy.

426
00:22:30,635 --> 00:22:31,935
You knew the end game.

427
00:22:32,068 --> 00:22:33,173
These animals,

428
00:22:33,308 --> 00:22:35,814
can replace thousands
of boots on the ground.

429
00:22:35,892 --> 00:22:37,401
How many lives would that save?

430
00:22:40,280 --> 00:22:41,566
War is part of nature.

431
00:22:43,500 --> 00:22:44,810
Look around, Owen.

432
00:22:45,234 --> 00:22:46,744
Every living thing in this jungle

433
00:22:47,405 --> 00:22:48,871
is trying to murder the other.

434
00:22:49,358 --> 00:22:50,524
Mother Nature is way of...

435
00:22:50,805 --> 00:22:52,049
testing her creations.

436
00:22:52,391 --> 00:22:53,871
Refining the pecking order.

437
00:22:54,640 --> 00:22:55,863
War is a struggle.

438
00:22:56,526 --> 00:22:57,753
Struggle breeds greatness.

439
00:22:59,054 --> 00:22:59,940
Without that,

440
00:23:00,160 --> 00:23:01,493
we end up with places like this,

441
00:23:01,517 --> 00:23:03,050
charge seven bucks a soda.

442
00:23:04,493 --> 00:23:06,302
Do you hear yourself when you talk?

443
00:23:09,800 --> 00:23:11,044
This is gonna happen.

444
00:23:12,082 --> 00:23:13,402
With or without you boys.

445
00:23:14,120 --> 00:23:15,451
Progress always wins, man.

446
00:23:16,320 --> 00:23:18,132
Maybe progress should lose for once.

447
00:23:20,400 --> 00:23:21,599
Pig loose!

448
00:23:22,320 --> 00:23:23,799
Pig loose!

449
00:23:42,019 --> 00:23:43,041
Owen, no!

450
00:23:46,560 --> 00:23:48,193
No, hold. No hold your fire!

451
00:23:49,920 --> 00:23:52,207
Hold your fire.
Do not fire.

452
00:23:54,780 --> 00:23:57,620
Put 12 amps in these animals,
they are never gonna trust me again.

453
00:23:59,833 --> 00:24:00,552
Blue.

454
00:24:01,422 --> 00:24:02,293
Stand down.

455
00:24:04,040 --> 00:24:04,920
Stand down.

456
00:24:06,279 --> 00:24:07,159
Hey! Hey!

457
00:24:07,357 --> 00:24:08,500
What did I just say?

458
00:24:09,840 --> 00:24:10,604
Delta.

459
00:24:10,628 --> 00:24:12,379
I see you.
Back up!

460
00:24:14,606 --> 00:24:15,346
Ok.

461
00:24:15,860 --> 00:24:16,786
Good.

462
00:24:18,040 --> 00:24:18,786
Good.

463
00:24:19,940 --> 00:24:20,813
Charlie?

464
00:24:22,566 --> 00:24:23,560
Stay right there.

465
00:24:25,000 --> 00:24:25,806
Good.

466
00:24:28,559 --> 00:24:29,420
Close the gate.

467
00:24:30,040 --> 00:24:31,133
Are you crazy?

468
00:24:31,375 --> 00:24:32,486
Ok. Just trust me.

469
00:24:32,873 --> 00:24:33,954
Close the gate!

470
00:24:36,507 --> 00:24:37,313
Shit.

471
00:24:47,726 --> 00:24:48,793
I am ok.

472
00:24:50,695 --> 00:24:52,129
You should have let them eat him.

473
00:24:52,520 --> 00:24:53,149
Yeah.

474
00:24:58,600 --> 00:24:59,726
You are the new guy, right?

475
00:25:00,596 --> 00:25:01,401
Yeah.

476
00:25:01,613 --> 00:25:03,899
You ever wonder
why there was a job opening?

477
00:25:06,106 --> 00:25:06,812
Hey.

478
00:25:07,280 --> 00:25:08,699
Don't ever turn your back to the cage.

479
00:25:53,720 --> 00:25:55,400
Lift me up.
I can't see!

480
00:25:56,040 --> 00:25:57,960
I am not Dad.
And you are not five.

481
00:25:58,926 --> 00:26:00,589
I can still ride the Triceratops.

482
00:26:00,613 --> 00:26:02,079
I am 47-and-a-half inches.

483
00:26:02,720 --> 00:26:04,433
This place is for little kids.

484
00:26:05,760 --> 00:26:06,760
Yeah, I know.

485
00:26:06,800 --> 00:26:08,933
Wanna go on the spinning dinosaur eggs?
Nope.

486
00:26:10,513 --> 00:26:11,826
Cover up your dork pouch.

487
00:26:12,640 --> 00:26:14,220
Because it's my wedding.

488
00:26:14,386 --> 00:26:16,361
No, Alec is not having a bachelor party.

489
00:26:16,746 --> 00:26:18,246
Because all his friends are animals.

490
00:26:18,878 --> 00:26:19,983
Scatter.
What?

491
00:26:20,073 --> 00:26:21,518
Go. Run. Go! Go! Go!

492
00:26:26,960 --> 00:26:27,961
Yuck!

493
00:26:39,647 --> 00:26:42,200
<i>Happy hour to Margarita Tour.</i>

494
00:26:43,000 --> 00:26:44,593
<i>The next T-Rex feeding</i>

495
00:26:44,618 --> 00:26:46,133
<i>will begin in 10 minutes.</i>
T-Rex! Come on, man!

496
00:26:46,158 --> 00:26:48,566
<i>Please make your way for this T-Rex event.</i>
Come on! Let's go!

497
00:26:48,680 --> 00:26:49,888
<i>Parents be aware,</i>

498
00:26:49,964 --> 00:26:52,766
<i>this show may be disturbing
for smaller children.</i>

499
00:27:04,560 --> 00:27:05,326
Hey, Mom.

500
00:27:06,146 --> 00:27:08,033
<i>You were supposed to call me
when you landed.</i>

501
00:27:09,040 --> 00:27:10,166
Are you having fun?

502
00:27:10,360 --> 00:27:10,951
<i>Yeah.</i>

503
00:27:11,248 --> 00:27:12,266
<i>I guess.</i>

504
00:27:13,840 --> 00:27:16,406
Aunt Claire gave us passes,
so we don't have to wait in line.

505
00:27:16,880 --> 00:27:18,245
Wait, she is not with you?

506
00:27:24,400 --> 00:27:25,401
Hey, Karen!

507
00:27:25,666 --> 00:27:27,219
<i>Hi, Claire. How is it going?</i>

508
00:27:28,160 --> 00:27:30,424
Yeah, everything is great.
The boys are having fun.

509
00:27:30,449 --> 00:27:31,179
<i>Everyone is...</i>

510
00:27:31,569 --> 00:27:32,622
<i>Yeah, everyone is good.</i>

511
00:27:33,085 --> 00:27:34,685
Really?
Because I just hung up with Zach,

512
00:27:34,710 --> 00:27:36,382
and he said
that you weren't even with them.

513
00:27:37,800 --> 00:27:38,720
Yeah, look.

514
00:27:39,450 --> 00:27:42,150
Today turned out to be
a really bad day for me.

515
00:27:42,257 --> 00:27:42,864
<i>And...</i>

516
00:27:43,200 --> 00:27:44,401
<i>They are in great hands.</i>

517
00:27:44,783 --> 00:27:45,808
<i>They are with my assistant.</i>

518
00:27:45,833 --> 00:27:47,571
<i>She is British so...</i>

519
00:27:47,854 --> 00:27:49,326
<i>they invented nannies.</i>

520
00:27:52,360 --> 00:27:53,600
Wait, are you crying?

521
00:27:55,139 --> 00:27:57,520
This was supposed to be
a family weekend, Claire.

522
00:27:58,080 --> 00:27:59,828
You have not seen
the boys in forever and

523
00:27:59,853 --> 00:28:02,080
and I know how Zach will treat Gray
if they are by themselves.

524
00:28:02,104 --> 00:28:03,706
And he can just be so mean.

525
00:28:04,126 --> 00:28:05,380
Ok, I am...

526
00:28:05,710 --> 00:28:06,832
I am sorry...

527
00:28:07,360 --> 00:28:08,675
<i>Tomorrow, I am gonna spend</i>

528
00:28:08,699 --> 00:28:09,865
<i>the entire day with them.</i>

529
00:28:09,890 --> 00:28:12,240
<i>I am going to take off work,
and I will not leave their side.</i>

530
00:28:12,266 --> 00:28:13,179
I promise.

531
00:28:13,560 --> 00:28:15,355
<i>Well, a promise tomorrow is worth</i>

532
00:28:15,380 --> 00:28:16,686
a lot less than trying today.

533
00:28:17,773 --> 00:28:19,626
You are using Mom's lines now?

534
00:28:20,099 --> 00:28:21,786
Oh, my God.
I am using Mom's lines.

535
00:28:22,560 --> 00:28:24,413
I am sorry but you know,
I have to tell you they work.

536
00:28:24,590 --> 00:28:26,136
<i>You will see when you have kids.</i>

537
00:28:26,360 --> 00:28:27,441
Yeah if.

538
00:28:27,904 --> 00:28:29,029
When...

539
00:28:30,030 --> 00:28:31,008
It's worth it.

540
00:28:31,480 --> 00:28:32,923
Bye, Mom.

541
00:28:35,560 --> 00:28:36,317
Bye.

542
00:28:54,120 --> 00:28:55,464
What do they want now?

543
00:28:56,180 --> 00:28:57,227
Mr. Grady?

544
00:28:58,200 --> 00:28:59,893
I need you to come...

545
00:29:00,736 --> 00:29:01,993
take a look at something.

546
00:29:03,500 --> 00:29:05,154
Why are you calling me Mr. Grady?

547
00:29:05,800 --> 00:29:06,628
Owen.

548
00:29:08,640 --> 00:29:09,766
If you are not too busy.

549
00:29:10,061 --> 00:29:11,015
I am pretty busy.

550
00:29:11,333 --> 00:29:12,610
We have an attraction.

551
00:29:12,680 --> 00:29:14,603
That's not what you said
the last time I saw you.

552
00:29:14,680 --> 00:29:16,451
I am talking about the dinosaurs,

553
00:29:16,609 --> 00:29:17,853
Mr. Grady.
Owen.

554
00:29:18,042 --> 00:29:19,621
A new species we have...

555
00:29:20,291 --> 00:29:21,161
made.

556
00:29:24,100 --> 00:29:26,326
You just went and made a new dinosaur?

557
00:29:26,920 --> 00:29:29,253
Yeah, it's kind of what we do here.

558
00:29:30,120 --> 00:29:32,118
The exhibit opens to the public
in three weeks.

559
00:29:32,224 --> 00:29:33,426
Mr. Masrani,

560
00:29:33,557 --> 00:29:35,571
wanted me to consult with you.

561
00:29:36,200 --> 00:29:38,178
You wanna consult here or...

562
00:29:39,286 --> 00:29:40,468
in my bungalow?

563
00:29:41,607 --> 00:29:42,712
That's not funny.

564
00:29:43,799 --> 00:29:44,839
A little funny.

565
00:29:44,864 --> 00:29:48,119
We would like you to evaluate
the paddock for vulnerabilities.

566
00:29:48,185 --> 00:29:49,059
Why me?

567
00:29:50,316 --> 00:29:53,195
I guess Mr. Masrani thinks,

568
00:29:53,626 --> 00:29:56,169
since you are able
to control the Raptors...

569
00:29:56,287 --> 00:29:58,082
It's all about control with you.

570
00:29:58,113 --> 00:30:00,729
I don't control the Raptors.
It's a relationship.

571
00:30:01,593 --> 00:30:03,153
It's based on mutual respect.

572
00:30:04,866 --> 00:30:06,706
That's why you and I
never had a second date.

573
00:30:06,960 --> 00:30:08,366
Excuse me?

574
00:30:08,391 --> 00:30:09,948
I never wanted a second date.

575
00:30:09,973 --> 00:30:12,035
Who prints out an itinerary
for a night out?

576
00:30:12,060 --> 00:30:13,741
I am an organized person.

577
00:30:13,766 --> 00:30:16,046
What kind of a diet
doesn't allow tequila?

578
00:30:16,266 --> 00:30:17,804
All of them, actually.

579
00:30:18,159 --> 00:30:20,307
And what kind of a man shows
up to a date,

580
00:30:20,585 --> 00:30:21,892
in board shorts?

581
00:30:22,440 --> 00:30:23,685
It's Central America. It's hot.

582
00:30:23,709 --> 00:30:25,103
Ok. Ok. Can we just...

583
00:30:25,307 --> 00:30:27,387
focus on the asset, please?

584
00:30:27,513 --> 00:30:28,527
The asset?

585
00:30:29,880 --> 00:30:30,916
Look, I get it.

586
00:30:31,841 --> 00:30:32,969
You are in charge out here.

587
00:30:32,994 --> 00:30:34,387
You gotta make
a lot of tough decisions.

588
00:30:34,412 --> 00:30:36,414
It's probably easier to pretend
these animals are just...

589
00:30:36,596 --> 00:30:37,898
numbers on a spreadsheet.

590
00:30:38,160 --> 00:30:39,100
But they are not.

591
00:30:40,148 --> 00:30:41,040
They are alive.

592
00:30:41,680 --> 00:30:43,320
I am fully aware they are alive.

593
00:30:43,720 --> 00:30:45,123
You might have made them
in a test tube,

594
00:30:45,277 --> 00:30:46,535
but they don't know that.

595
00:30:46,773 --> 00:30:48,653
They are thinking, I gotta eat.

596
00:30:49,360 --> 00:30:50,346
I gotta hunt.

597
00:30:51,412 --> 00:30:52,249
I gotta...

598
00:30:54,418 --> 00:30:56,092
You can relate to at least,

599
00:30:56,957 --> 00:30:58,024
one of those things.

600
00:30:58,173 --> 00:30:58,958
Right?

601
00:31:02,760 --> 00:31:03,921
I will be in the car.

602
00:31:07,908 --> 00:31:09,615
You might want to change your shirt.

603
00:31:10,319 --> 00:31:12,067
They are very sensitive...

604
00:31:12,197 --> 00:31:13,299
to smell.

605
00:31:23,377 --> 00:31:24,424
<i>The Mosasaurus</i>

606
00:31:24,449 --> 00:31:27,147
<i>was thought to have hunted
near the surface of the water</i>

607
00:31:27,172 --> 00:31:30,543
<i>where it preyed on anything
it could sink its teeth into,</i>

608
00:31:30,733 --> 00:31:32,504
<i>including turtles,</i>

609
00:31:32,634 --> 00:31:33,755
<i>large fish,</i>

610
00:31:33,885 --> 00:31:35,360
<i>even smaller Mosasaurs.</i>

611
00:31:36,460 --> 00:31:37,592
<i>Ok folks,</i>

612
00:31:37,616 --> 00:31:40,848
<i>let's see if she is still hungry
after already eating today.</i>

613
00:31:41,560 --> 00:31:43,473
<i>She is a little shy,</i>

614
00:31:43,497 --> 00:31:44,678
<i>so be nice,</i>
Zach.

615
00:31:44,703 --> 00:31:46,423
<i>And give her a hand
when she comes out.</i>

616
00:31:46,448 --> 00:31:46,990
Zach!

617
00:31:47,440 --> 00:31:48,440
<i>The Mosasaurus!</i>

618
00:32:00,520 --> 00:32:03,046
Oh, my God!
That was awesome!

619
00:32:06,426 --> 00:32:07,426
<i>Hold on tight.</i>

620
00:32:07,520 --> 00:32:09,541
<i>We are gonna give you
an even closer look</i>

621
00:32:09,565 --> 00:32:11,120
<i>at our Mosasaurus.</i>

622
00:32:25,687 --> 00:32:27,177
It had 88 teeth!

623
00:32:29,400 --> 00:32:31,613
Wanna see something else cool?
Yeah!

624
00:32:39,080 --> 00:32:40,155
We have been,

625
00:32:40,179 --> 00:32:42,126
pre-booking tickets for months.

626
00:32:42,513 --> 00:32:45,475
The park needs a new attraction
every few years

627
00:32:45,500 --> 00:32:47,487
in order to reinvigorate
the public's interest.

628
00:32:47,661 --> 00:32:49,294
Kind of like the space program.

629
00:32:49,641 --> 00:32:53,215
Corporate felt genetic modification
would up the wow factor.

630
00:32:53,340 --> 00:32:55,020
They are dinosaurs.
Wow enough.

631
00:32:55,613 --> 00:32:57,767
Not according to our focus groups.

632
00:32:57,840 --> 00:33:00,126
The Indominus Rex
makes us relevant again.

633
00:33:00,151 --> 00:33:02,341
The Indominus Rex?

634
00:33:02,366 --> 00:33:04,095
We needed something scary

635
00:33:04,119 --> 00:33:05,415
and easy to pronounce.

636
00:33:05,440 --> 00:33:07,001
You should hear a four-year-old

637
00:33:07,026 --> 00:33:09,060
try to say Archaeornithomimus.

638
00:33:09,420 --> 00:33:10,973
You should hear you try to say it.

639
00:33:16,880 --> 00:33:18,120
So what is this thing made of?

640
00:33:19,200 --> 00:33:21,112
The base genome is a T-Rex.

641
00:33:21,136 --> 00:33:22,405
The rest is...

642
00:33:22,820 --> 00:33:23,833
classified.

643
00:33:24,040 --> 00:33:26,771
You made a new dinosaur,
but you don't even know what it is?

644
00:33:26,919 --> 00:33:28,813
The lab delivers us finished assets,

645
00:33:28,838 --> 00:33:30,555
and we show them to the public.

646
00:33:30,580 --> 00:33:32,233
Can we drop a steer, please?

647
00:33:32,666 --> 00:33:34,380
How long has the animal been in here?

648
00:33:35,124 --> 00:33:36,210
All its life.

649
00:33:36,480 --> 00:33:38,604
Never seen anything
outside of these walls?

650
00:33:38,880 --> 00:33:40,420
We can't exactly walk it.

651
00:33:40,466 --> 00:33:41,870
And you feed it with that?

652
00:33:47,120 --> 00:33:48,419
Is there a problem?

653
00:33:49,040 --> 00:33:52,065
Animals raised in isolation are not
always the most functional.

654
00:33:53,080 --> 00:33:55,468
Your Raptors are born in captivity.

655
00:33:55,960 --> 00:33:57,023
With siblings.

656
00:33:57,655 --> 00:33:59,109
They learn social skills.

657
00:33:59,520 --> 00:34:01,342
And I imprint on them
when they are born.

658
00:34:01,482 --> 00:34:02,468
There is trust.

659
00:34:02,780 --> 00:34:06,427
The only positive relationship
this animal has is with that crane.

660
00:34:07,920 --> 00:34:09,460
At least she knows that means food.

661
00:34:09,633 --> 00:34:12,197
So, she needs a friend.

662
00:34:12,512 --> 00:34:14,816
We should schedule play-dates?
That sort of thing?

663
00:34:16,239 --> 00:34:17,584
Probably not a good idea.

664
00:34:22,000 --> 00:34:23,000
Where is it?

665
00:34:23,320 --> 00:34:24,481
Is it in the basement?

666
00:34:24,767 --> 00:34:26,052
Is there a downstairs?

667
00:34:26,700 --> 00:34:28,135
Maybe it's in the rec room.

668
00:34:28,160 --> 00:34:30,240
It was just here.
We were just here.

669
00:34:39,160 --> 00:34:40,659
Oh, shit.

670
00:34:43,720 --> 00:34:45,299
That doesn't make any sense.

671
00:34:47,800 --> 00:34:49,586
These doors have not
been opened in weeks.

672
00:34:51,400 --> 00:34:53,046
Were those claw marks always there?

673
00:34:58,840 --> 00:35:00,054
Do you think it...

674
00:35:03,680 --> 00:35:04,573
Oh, God.

675
00:35:05,720 --> 00:35:07,370
She has an implant in her back.

676
00:35:07,533 --> 00:35:09,333
I can track it from the control room.

677
00:35:19,880 --> 00:35:21,695
We have an asset out of containment.

678
00:35:21,720 --> 00:35:23,192
Put ACU on alert.

679
00:35:23,216 --> 00:35:24,427
This is not a drill.

680
00:35:25,073 --> 00:35:27,413
Even though I didn't meet him
until I was 13,

681
00:35:27,506 --> 00:35:29,125
I definitely consider Carl to be,

682
00:35:29,246 --> 00:35:30,771
more of a dad than my real dad.
Yeah.

683
00:35:35,440 --> 00:35:36,372
Yeah, hello?

684
00:35:36,396 --> 00:35:37,329
<i>Lowery.</i>

685
00:35:37,480 --> 00:35:39,164
Get me coordinates on the Indominus.

686
00:35:40,619 --> 00:35:41,466
Ok, yeah.

687
00:35:43,133 --> 00:35:44,419
I am doing it right now.

688
00:36:08,526 --> 00:36:10,153
That wall is 40 feet high.

689
00:36:10,746 --> 00:36:12,346
Do you really think
she could have climbed out?

690
00:36:13,440 --> 00:36:14,406
It depends.

691
00:36:15,440 --> 00:36:16,406
On what?

692
00:36:17,240 --> 00:36:19,913
What kind of dinosaur
they cooked up in that lab.

693
00:36:22,220 --> 00:36:23,380
Wait, what the hell?

694
00:36:24,280 --> 00:36:25,613
It's in the cage.

695
00:36:26,120 --> 00:36:28,406
No, that's impossible.
I was just there.

696
00:36:28,487 --> 00:36:30,655
Claire, I am telling you, she is in the cage.

697
00:36:32,000 --> 00:36:33,133
Wait a sec...

698
00:36:33,466 --> 00:36:34,586
There are people in there.

699
00:36:36,960 --> 00:36:38,360
Get them out of there now.

700
00:36:39,480 --> 00:36:40,140
Now!

701
00:36:40,333 --> 00:36:41,813
Paddock 11, this is Control.

702
00:36:41,837 --> 00:36:43,893
You need to evacuate
the containment area.

703
00:36:44,333 --> 00:36:45,320
<i>Paddock 11.</i>

704
00:36:46,360 --> 00:36:47,906
<i>Paddock 11, do you copy?</i>

705
00:36:48,793 --> 00:36:49,794
Yeah, what is the problem?

706
00:36:49,840 --> 00:36:51,640
It's in the cage!
It's in there with you!

707
00:36:51,780 --> 00:36:52,500
Go!

708
00:37:22,280 --> 00:37:23,171
Close the door.

709
00:37:23,486 --> 00:37:25,266
We can't lock him in there with that thing.
Close it now!

710
00:37:25,584 --> 00:37:26,665
<i>Somebody talk to me!</i>

711
00:37:26,690 --> 00:37:27,891
What is happening?

712
00:37:29,920 --> 00:37:30,968
Shit!

713
00:39:41,186 --> 00:39:42,034
Everyone...

714
00:39:42,291 --> 00:39:43,244
remain...

715
00:39:43,628 --> 00:39:44,454
calm.

716
00:39:53,106 --> 00:39:56,553
The implant will shock it
if it gets too close to a perimeter fence.

717
00:39:56,600 --> 00:39:58,090
Ok. It's moving really fast.

718
00:39:58,160 --> 00:40:00,003
This is Control.
Put out a park-wide alert.

719
00:40:00,028 --> 00:40:01,466
Hang up that damn phone, please.

720
00:40:02,200 --> 00:40:04,574
Sorry, I am getting new information.
Everything is fine.

721
00:40:04,599 --> 00:40:06,593
Let Asset Containment capture it quietly.

722
00:40:07,120 --> 00:40:09,226
The very existence of this park

723
00:40:09,377 --> 00:40:12,259
is predicated on our ability
to handle incidents like this.

724
00:40:12,580 --> 00:40:14,249
It was an eventuality, ok?

725
00:40:14,320 --> 00:40:16,020
You should put that in the brochure.

726
00:40:16,260 --> 00:40:17,528
Eventually,

727
00:40:17,552 --> 00:40:19,607
one of these things will eat somebody.

728
00:40:19,807 --> 00:40:22,986
That paddock is four miles
from the closest attraction.

729
00:40:23,240 --> 00:40:24,493
ACU can handle this.

730
00:40:24,517 --> 00:40:25,767
No one else is gonna get...

731
00:40:25,792 --> 00:40:26,570
Eaten?

732
00:40:32,826 --> 00:40:33,878
<i>To all units.</i>

733
00:40:34,175 --> 00:40:35,861
<i>This is a non-lethal operation.</i>

734
00:40:35,885 --> 00:40:37,070
<i>Understood?</i>

735
00:40:39,779 --> 00:40:40,959
Be sweet. Calm.

736
00:40:41,706 --> 00:40:42,752
Calm. Be sweet.

737
00:40:43,078 --> 00:40:44,798
Be sweet.
How fast can they run?

738
00:40:45,734 --> 00:40:46,625
Forty.

739
00:40:47,399 --> 00:40:48,673
Fifty when they are hungry.

740
00:40:50,600 --> 00:40:52,633
You ever open them up,
see what they can do?

741
00:40:53,680 --> 00:40:54,453
No.

742
00:40:55,280 --> 00:40:56,120
Oh, shit!

743
00:40:57,213 --> 00:40:59,153
That got me.
It got me.

744
00:40:59,700 --> 00:41:00,738
What do you think?

745
00:41:01,013 --> 00:41:02,086
Want to take one home?

746
00:41:02,200 --> 00:41:03,280
Hey, don't joke.

747
00:41:04,246 --> 00:41:05,466
When I was your age,

748
00:41:06,087 --> 00:41:07,900
I rescued a wolf pup.

749
00:41:09,539 --> 00:41:10,915
It was, like, two months old.

750
00:41:10,939 --> 00:41:12,019
It could barely walk.

751
00:41:13,206 --> 00:41:14,656
It used to sleep by my bed.

752
00:41:14,820 --> 00:41:15,880
Watch over me.

753
00:41:17,580 --> 00:41:19,131
My wife, she came at me with a...

754
00:41:19,513 --> 00:41:20,526
steak knife.

755
00:41:21,360 --> 00:41:22,633
It took a chunk out of her arm.

756
00:41:23,566 --> 00:41:24,533
Did you put him down?

757
00:41:25,520 --> 00:41:26,359
Hell, no.

758
00:41:28,272 --> 00:41:29,058
We had an...

759
00:41:29,305 --> 00:41:30,895
unshakeable bond, you know?

760
00:41:31,326 --> 00:41:32,678
Just like you and...

761
00:41:34,606 --> 00:41:35,612
What's his name?

762
00:41:36,626 --> 00:41:37,441
Delta.

763
00:41:38,045 --> 00:41:39,166
And she is a girl.

764
00:41:40,293 --> 00:41:41,294
Can I...

765
00:42:00,147 --> 00:42:00,967
Shit.

766
00:42:01,980 --> 00:42:02,999
Code 19!

767
00:42:03,200 --> 00:42:04,361
That's the new one!

768
00:42:04,540 --> 00:42:05,799
They said we lost two guys!

769
00:42:05,965 --> 00:42:07,220
What's a Code 19?

770
00:42:07,618 --> 00:42:09,005
Asset out of containment.

771
00:42:10,233 --> 00:42:11,183
These people,

772
00:42:11,273 --> 00:42:12,428
they never learn.

773
00:42:14,233 --> 00:42:17,260
They are gonna learn all kinds of things
about their new asset now.

774
00:42:20,706 --> 00:42:21,861
Hey. Yeah, it's me.

775
00:42:22,880 --> 00:42:24,700
We might have an opportunity here.

776
00:42:43,640 --> 00:42:44,839
You guys been here before?

777
00:42:48,026 --> 00:42:49,321
If Mom and Dad get divorced,

778
00:42:49,346 --> 00:42:51,295
will one of us be with Mom
and the other with Dad?

779
00:42:51,320 --> 00:42:52,113
What?

780
00:42:52,737 --> 00:42:53,853
Why would you say that?

781
00:42:53,967 --> 00:42:54,906
Because they are.

782
00:42:54,953 --> 00:42:56,520
No, they are not getting...

783
00:42:56,544 --> 00:42:58,017
they are not getting divorced.

784
00:42:59,510 --> 00:43:01,703
Look. You have not been around long enough.
They have always been that way.

785
00:43:02,675 --> 00:43:04,359
They get mail from two different lawyers.

786
00:43:04,384 --> 00:43:05,686
That doesn't mean anything.

787
00:43:06,080 --> 00:43:08,106
I googled.
They are divorce lawyers.

788
00:43:11,880 --> 00:43:13,610
Alright, whatever.
You know what?

789
00:43:14,164 --> 00:43:14,997
It doesn't matter.

790
00:43:15,330 --> 00:43:17,344
Ok? I am gonna be gone
in two years anyway.

791
00:43:17,369 --> 00:43:20,077
I mean, all my friends
parents are divorced and...

792
00:43:22,466 --> 00:43:23,600
Hey, knock it off.

793
00:43:24,966 --> 00:43:26,172
You are gonna cry?

794
00:43:28,006 --> 00:43:29,512
Look, you are gonna get
two of everything.

795
00:43:29,846 --> 00:43:33,052
Right, you are gonna get two birthdays,
two Thanksgivings, two...

796
00:43:33,180 --> 00:43:34,692
I don't want two of everything.

797
00:43:35,720 --> 00:43:37,066
Yeah, well it's not up to you.

798
00:43:38,326 --> 00:43:40,233
Alright, there is a point
you have to grow up.

799
00:44:11,600 --> 00:44:12,847
I need to see a badge.

800
00:44:12,871 --> 00:44:14,849
Sir, sir. I need to see a badge.
What the hell happened out there?

801
00:44:14,874 --> 00:44:15,368
Sir.

802
00:44:15,393 --> 00:44:17,486
There are thermal cameras
all over that paddock.

803
00:44:17,600 --> 00:44:19,126
She did not just disappear!

804
00:44:21,120 --> 00:44:22,606
It must have been some kind of a...

805
00:44:22,846 --> 00:44:24,680
technical malfunction.
Were you not watching?

806
00:44:25,260 --> 00:44:27,208
She marked up that wall as a distraction.

807
00:44:27,233 --> 00:44:28,650
She wanted us to think she escaped!

808
00:44:28,675 --> 00:44:30,744
Hold on.
We are talking about an animal here.

809
00:44:30,769 --> 00:44:32,848
A highly intelligent animal.

810
00:44:32,873 --> 00:44:34,068
400 meters to the beacon.

811
00:44:58,073 --> 00:45:00,175
You are going after her with non-lethals.

812
00:45:00,200 --> 00:45:04,106
We have $26 million invested in that asset.
We can't just kill it.

813
00:45:04,526 --> 00:45:05,738
Those men are gonna die.

814
00:45:05,763 --> 00:45:07,078
300 meters to the beacon.

815
00:45:07,120 --> 00:45:08,439
You need to call this mission off right now.

816
00:45:08,464 --> 00:45:09,939
They are right on top of it.
Call it off...

817
00:45:10,132 --> 00:45:12,371
right now.
You are not in control here!

818
00:45:44,933 --> 00:45:46,249
Blood is not clotted yet.

819
00:45:46,466 --> 00:45:47,639
<i>It's close.</i>

820
00:45:48,760 --> 00:45:50,073
What is that?

821
00:45:51,680 --> 00:45:53,950
That's her tracking implant.
She clawed it out.

822
00:45:54,553 --> 00:45:56,124
How would it know to do that?

823
00:45:57,986 --> 00:45:59,743
She remembered where they put it in.

824
00:46:33,200 --> 00:46:34,862
It can camouflage!

825
00:47:31,360 --> 00:47:32,834
Evacuate the island.

826
00:47:34,280 --> 00:47:35,654
We would never reopen.

827
00:47:36,466 --> 00:47:38,635
You made a genetic hybrid,

828
00:47:39,105 --> 00:47:40,808
raised it in captivity.

829
00:47:40,833 --> 00:47:43,273
She is seeing all of this for the first time.

830
00:47:43,339 --> 00:47:45,910
She does not even know what she is.

831
00:47:46,200 --> 00:47:48,466
She will kill everything that moves.

832
00:47:49,080 --> 00:47:51,810
Do you think the animal
is contemplating its own existence?

833
00:47:51,880 --> 00:47:53,742
She is learning where
she fits in the food chain,

834
00:47:53,767 --> 00:47:55,815
and I am not sure
you want her to figure that out.

835
00:47:56,330 --> 00:47:57,696
Now, Asset Containment

836
00:47:57,720 --> 00:48:00,105
can use live ammunition
in an emergency situation.

837
00:48:00,130 --> 00:48:02,091
You have an M134 in your armory.

838
00:48:02,116 --> 00:48:04,232
Put it on a chopper
and smoke this thing!

839
00:48:04,257 --> 00:48:05,372
We have families here.

840
00:48:05,397 --> 00:48:07,590
I am not gonna turn this place
into some kind of a war zone.

841
00:48:07,615 --> 00:48:08,770
You already have.

842
00:48:08,800 --> 00:48:10,459
Mr. Grady, if you are not gonna help,

843
00:48:10,483 --> 00:48:12,173
there is no reason for you to be in here.

844
00:48:19,080 --> 00:48:20,219
I would have a word

845
00:48:20,372 --> 00:48:21,799
with your people in the lab.

846
00:48:22,573 --> 00:48:23,746
That thing out there,

847
00:48:24,933 --> 00:48:26,126
that's no dinosaur.

848
00:48:42,480 --> 00:48:43,287
Ok.

849
00:48:45,392 --> 00:48:48,394
I am going to close everything
north of the resort.

850
00:48:48,906 --> 00:48:52,319
This is a Phase One, real world.
Bring everyone in.

851
00:48:52,387 --> 00:48:54,274
This is a Phase One, real world.

852
00:48:54,299 --> 00:48:57,125
I repeat, this is a Phase One.
Bring everyone back in.

853
00:48:59,920 --> 00:49:00,843
Did you know,

854
00:49:00,868 --> 00:49:02,469
the soft tissue is preserved,

855
00:49:02,493 --> 00:49:03,959
because the iron in the dinosaur's blood

856
00:49:03,984 --> 00:49:05,222
generates free radicals,

857
00:49:05,246 --> 00:49:06,859
and those are highly reactive.

858
00:49:06,919 --> 00:49:09,926
So, the proteins and the cell
membranes get all mixed up,

859
00:49:09,952 --> 00:49:12,366
and act as a natural preservative.

860
00:49:12,660 --> 00:49:14,528
DNA can survive for millennia that way.

861
00:49:14,833 --> 00:49:16,942
See now, even if the amber mines dry up,

862
00:49:17,021 --> 00:49:18,226
they will still have bones...
Shut up.

863
00:49:21,680 --> 00:49:24,286
What do you think's gonna happen
from you just staring at them?

864
00:49:27,273 --> 00:49:28,093
Thanks man.

865
00:49:28,440 --> 00:49:29,305
You are welcome.

866
00:49:32,006 --> 00:49:32,999
Enjoy the ride.

867
00:49:37,520 --> 00:49:39,720
<i>Pregnant women and those
who suffer from motion sickness</i>

868
00:49:39,757 --> 00:49:42,044
<i>should consult with a doctor
before riding this ride.</i>

869
00:49:54,480 --> 00:49:55,600
Enjoy the ride.

870
00:49:59,000 --> 00:49:59,726
Hello?

871
00:50:03,060 --> 00:50:03,910
Seriously?

872
00:50:06,270 --> 00:50:08,170
Sorry, folks. The ride is closed.

873
00:50:09,160 --> 00:50:13,449
Everyone needs to proceed to
the monorail and exit towards the...

874
00:50:17,080 --> 00:50:18,521
Come on guys, I just work here.

875
00:50:19,253 --> 00:50:20,964
<i>Due to technical difficulties,</i>

876
00:50:21,047 --> 00:50:23,159
<i>all our exhibits are now closed.</i>

877
00:50:31,033 --> 00:50:32,512
You know that I am not at liberty

878
00:50:32,537 --> 00:50:34,574
to reveal the asset's genetic makeup.

879
00:50:35,346 --> 00:50:37,668
Modified animals are
known to be unpredictable.

880
00:50:38,846 --> 00:50:40,301
It's killed people, Henry.

881
00:50:41,879 --> 00:50:42,921
That's unfortunate.

882
00:50:43,959 --> 00:50:47,051
What purpose could we have
for a dinosaur that can camouflage?

883
00:50:47,631 --> 00:50:49,133
Cuttlefish genes were added

884
00:50:49,158 --> 00:50:52,375
to help her withstand
an accelerated growth rate.

885
00:50:52,522 --> 00:50:56,702
Cuttlefish have chromatophores
that allow the skin to change color.

886
00:50:57,639 --> 00:50:59,455
It hid from thermal technology.

887
00:51:00,860 --> 00:51:01,561
Really?

888
00:51:02,073 --> 00:51:03,273
How is that possible?

889
00:51:07,520 --> 00:51:10,198
Tree frogs can modulate
their infrared output.

890
00:51:10,846 --> 00:51:12,724
We used strands from their DNA,

891
00:51:12,748 --> 00:51:14,851
to adapt her to a tropical climate but...

892
00:51:15,318 --> 00:51:16,468
I never imagined...

893
00:51:16,493 --> 00:51:17,986
Who authorized you to do this?

894
00:51:19,326 --> 00:51:20,180
You did.

895
00:51:20,986 --> 00:51:21,660
Bigger.

896
00:51:22,440 --> 00:51:23,280
Scarier.

897
00:51:24,673 --> 00:51:26,446
Cooler. I believe is the word...

898
00:51:26,576 --> 00:51:28,680
that you used in your memo.

899
00:51:29,613 --> 00:51:32,901
You cannot have an animal
with exaggerated predator features

900
00:51:32,926 --> 00:51:35,315
without the corresponding
behavioral traits.

901
00:51:35,660 --> 00:51:37,066
What you are doing here...

902
00:51:38,340 --> 00:51:39,546
What you have done.

903
00:51:41,360 --> 00:51:42,868
The Board will shut down this park,

904
00:51:42,893 --> 00:51:44,666
seize your work,
everything you have built.

905
00:51:46,534 --> 00:51:48,513
And Hammond won't be there
to protect you this time.

906
00:51:48,593 --> 00:51:50,429
All of this exists...

907
00:51:50,793 --> 00:51:52,000
because of me.

908
00:51:53,120 --> 00:51:54,683
If I don't innovate,

909
00:51:54,860 --> 00:51:56,162
somebody else will.

910
00:51:57,313 --> 00:52:00,595
You are to cease
all activities here immediately.

911
00:52:01,760 --> 00:52:05,285
You are acting like we are engaged
in some kind of mad science.

912
00:52:05,591 --> 00:52:08,071
But we are doing what we have done,

913
00:52:08,095 --> 00:52:09,257
from the beginning.

914
00:52:10,020 --> 00:52:12,904
Nothing in Jurassic World is natural.

915
00:52:13,084 --> 00:52:16,993
We have always filled gaps in the
genome with the DNA of other animals.

916
00:52:17,100 --> 00:52:19,480
And, if their genetic code was pure,

917
00:52:19,540 --> 00:52:21,095
many of them would look quite different.

918
00:52:21,120 --> 00:52:23,666
But you didn't ask for reality.
You asked for more teeth.

919
00:52:23,691 --> 00:52:25,134
I never asked for a monster!

920
00:52:25,159 --> 00:52:26,604
Monster is a relative term.

921
00:52:26,866 --> 00:52:29,249
To a canary, a cat is a monster.

922
00:52:30,306 --> 00:52:31,823
We are just used to being the cat.

923
00:52:37,080 --> 00:52:38,789
<i>Hey, there.
I am Jimmy Fallon.</i>

924
00:52:38,814 --> 00:52:40,459
<i>Welcome aboard the Gyrosphere,</i>

925
00:52:40,484 --> 00:52:42,940
<i>an amazing machine
made possible by science.</i>

926
00:52:43,146 --> 00:52:44,636
<i>Your safety is our main concern.</i>

927
00:52:44,760 --> 00:52:46,866
<i>Which is why you are behind
our invisible barrier system,</i>

928
00:52:46,957 --> 00:52:49,553
<i>which protects you from things
like Dilophosaurus venom.</i>

929
00:52:50,906 --> 00:52:52,366
<i>One drop of thiscan...</i>

930
00:52:52,390 --> 00:52:54,035
<i>paralyze you, so watch out.</i>

931
00:52:54,500 --> 00:52:55,369
<i>Is this real?</i>

932
00:52:55,973 --> 00:52:56,879
<i>It is?</i>

933
00:52:57,997 --> 00:52:59,328
<i>And for added protection,</i>

934
00:52:59,353 --> 00:53:02,400
<i>each vehicle is surrounded
by aluminum oxynitride glass.</i>

935
00:53:02,513 --> 00:53:03,418
<i>So tough,</i>

936
00:53:03,442 --> 00:53:05,437
<i>it can stop a 50-caliber bullet.</i>

937
00:53:09,148 --> 00:53:11,995
<i>The Gyroscopic technology
will keep you upright at all times...</i>

938
00:53:12,020 --> 00:53:14,287
Where are they?
<i>So you have got nothing to worry about.</i>

939
00:53:14,400 --> 00:53:15,333
Oh, man.

940
00:53:51,480 --> 00:53:55,326
<i>Due to technical difficulties
all our exhibits are now closed.</i>

941
00:53:55,480 --> 00:53:57,013
<i>Please disembark all rides,</i>

942
00:53:57,210 --> 00:53:58,513
<i>and return to the resort.</i>

943
00:54:01,886 --> 00:54:04,279
Come on, now we can stay out
a couple more minutes.

944
00:54:05,138 --> 00:54:06,822
But they said it was closed.

945
00:54:07,152 --> 00:54:09,141
Aunt Claire gave us
special wristbands, right?

946
00:54:09,273 --> 00:54:10,379
We are VIP, dude.

947
00:54:11,640 --> 00:54:12,487
Come on.

948
00:54:13,279 --> 00:54:14,120
It will be fun.

949
00:54:44,799 --> 00:54:45,826
<i>Hello?</i>
Zara.

950
00:54:46,880 --> 00:54:49,200
I need you to bring the boys
back to the hotel right away.

951
00:54:49,280 --> 00:54:51,123
<i>I don't know...
I have been looking everywhere for them.</i>

952
00:54:51,148 --> 00:54:52,694
<i>It's just been quite a while.</i>
Slow down.

953
00:54:52,718 --> 00:54:53,540
I can't hear you.

954
00:54:53,591 --> 00:54:54,904
<i>Zach and Gray, they have run off.</i>

955
00:54:54,929 --> 00:54:55,929
They what?

956
00:55:01,260 --> 00:55:02,120
Hey, Claire.

957
00:55:03,060 --> 00:55:04,247
Zach, thank God.

958
00:55:04,573 --> 00:55:05,610
Is Gray with you?

959
00:55:05,880 --> 00:55:07,501
I can't really hear you.

960
00:55:07,525 --> 00:55:09,126
We are in the hamster ball.

961
00:55:09,612 --> 00:55:11,000
Ok. Zach, listen to me.

962
00:55:11,240 --> 00:55:12,506
<i>I need you to...</i>

963
00:55:14,373 --> 00:55:15,201
Hello?

964
00:55:16,247 --> 00:55:17,113
<i>Hello?</i>
Zach?

965
00:55:21,648 --> 00:55:23,408
Are there any Gyrospheres
left in the Valley?

966
00:55:23,433 --> 00:55:25,048
No, they are all accounted for.
It's my job.

967
00:55:25,201 --> 00:55:25,802
What?

968
00:55:25,826 --> 00:55:27,421
There is one in the field.

969
00:55:28,520 --> 00:55:30,204
Send a team of rangers, bring them in.

970
00:55:30,280 --> 00:55:32,320
Security, we need a search
and rescue in the Valley.

971
00:55:32,344 --> 00:55:34,608
<i>It's gonna be a while.
We have got our hands full out here.</i>

972
00:55:35,582 --> 00:55:37,495
No, no, no, no, no,
there are two guests missing!

973
00:55:37,520 --> 00:55:39,495
You need to make this your top priority!

974
00:55:39,520 --> 00:55:40,641
Just do it, man.

975
00:55:40,760 --> 00:55:42,266
<i>There is a lot of guests missing.
We are doing the best we can.</i>

976
00:55:42,291 --> 00:55:43,704
Ok. Fine. I will do it myself.

977
00:55:44,480 --> 00:55:47,324
<i>Do you think I am the one
you need to be worried about right now?</i>

978
00:55:47,440 --> 00:55:48,560
<i>Back off!</i>

979
00:55:56,946 --> 00:55:58,072
What happened here?

980
00:56:01,600 --> 00:56:02,380
Dude.

981
00:56:03,520 --> 00:56:04,500
Off-road.

982
00:56:05,193 --> 00:56:06,633
But they told us to go back.

983
00:56:07,853 --> 00:56:10,833
I am just worried you are not getting
the full Jurassic World experience.

984
00:56:27,346 --> 00:56:28,113
Claire!

985
00:56:29,720 --> 00:56:30,667
I need you.

986
00:56:30,886 --> 00:56:31,507
Ok.

987
00:56:31,700 --> 00:56:33,086
I need your help. My nephews,

988
00:56:33,416 --> 00:56:34,315
they are out in the Valley.

989
00:56:34,340 --> 00:56:35,720
Please, if anything happens to them...

990
00:56:37,720 --> 00:56:38,546
How old?

991
00:56:39,413 --> 00:56:40,233
See...

992
00:56:40,713 --> 00:56:41,720
The older one he is like...

993
00:56:41,824 --> 00:56:43,766
he is high school age.
The younger one, he is...

994
00:56:44,700 --> 00:56:45,348
He is...

995
00:56:45,428 --> 00:56:47,566
a few years...
You don't know how old your nephews are?

996
00:56:49,580 --> 00:56:51,573
No, no.
Bad idea, bad idea.

997
00:56:51,660 --> 00:56:52,981
Great idea.
No!

998
00:56:53,681 --> 00:56:55,615
We are gonna get arrested.
They will shave our heads,

999
00:56:55,819 --> 00:56:57,653
and we are gonna have
to make root beer in the toilet.

1000
00:56:57,684 --> 00:56:58,843
What are you talking about?

1001
00:57:00,866 --> 00:57:01,597
There.

1002
00:57:03,399 --> 00:57:04,553
You see? I told you.

1003
00:57:06,286 --> 00:57:08,288
You are welcome. 
Up close and personal with...

1004
00:57:08,499 --> 00:57:09,247
four...

1005
00:57:10,339 --> 00:57:11,426
dinosauruses.

1006
00:57:11,719 --> 00:57:12,939
Ankylosaurus.

1007
00:57:13,566 --> 00:57:14,711
We should not be here.

1008
00:57:15,100 --> 00:57:16,580
And there is five dinosaurs.

1009
00:57:17,753 --> 00:57:19,676
Are not you supposed to be
a genius or something?

1010
00:57:19,701 --> 00:57:20,306
Look.

1011
00:57:20,613 --> 00:57:21,134
One.

1012
00:57:21,298 --> 00:57:21,843
Two.

1013
00:57:21,867 --> 00:57:22,433
Three.

1014
00:57:23,100 --> 00:57:23,746
Four.

1015
00:57:24,367 --> 00:57:24,993
Five.

1016
00:57:37,360 --> 00:57:38,850
Go, go, go!
Shit!

1017
00:57:48,286 --> 00:57:49,186
Hold it together, man!

1018
00:57:57,713 --> 00:57:59,319
Drive! Drive! Go!

1019
00:58:31,373 --> 00:58:32,420
We are safe in here, right?

1020
00:58:32,720 --> 00:58:34,060
Yeah. they are totally safe.

1021
00:58:39,243 --> 00:58:40,289
Come on.

1022
00:58:41,200 --> 00:58:42,132
Pick up.

1023
00:58:42,255 --> 00:58:43,615
Pick up, pick up, pick up.

1024
00:58:50,163 --> 00:58:50,761
Zach.

1025
00:58:51,210 --> 00:58:52,370
I almost got it.

1026
00:58:52,480 --> 00:58:53,561
Zach?
Yeah?

1027
00:58:53,927 --> 00:58:55,090
Look.
What?

1028
00:59:51,160 --> 00:59:52,200
Go! Go!

1029
00:59:57,646 --> 00:59:58,626
Gray, go!

1030
01:00:04,680 --> 01:00:05,841
Oh, crap!

1031
01:00:14,799 --> 01:00:16,185
We are gonna have to jump.
I can't.

1032
01:00:16,210 --> 01:00:17,685
Are you ready?
One, two...

1033
01:00:17,836 --> 01:00:18,797
Come on!

1034
01:01:09,760 --> 01:01:10,778
You jumped.

1035
01:01:31,519 --> 01:01:32,588
Stay in the car.

1036
01:02:03,640 --> 01:02:04,413
Hi.

1037
01:02:05,600 --> 01:02:06,420
Hi.

1038
01:02:20,000 --> 01:02:21,480
I know, I know.

1039
01:02:32,160 --> 01:02:33,372
It's alright.

1040
01:02:34,400 --> 01:02:35,580
Alright, girl.

1041
01:02:52,120 --> 01:02:52,819
Ok.

1042
01:02:53,060 --> 01:02:54,339
Ok. Ok. Ok.

1043
01:02:56,100 --> 01:02:56,993
You are ok.

1044
01:03:51,379 --> 01:03:52,411
It didn't eat them.

1045
01:03:54,453 --> 01:03:55,871
It's killing for sport.

1046
01:04:03,440 --> 01:04:05,249
Units on standby, ready for go.

1047
01:04:05,400 --> 01:04:07,500
Good. Hold off on that live feed.

1048
01:04:07,525 --> 01:04:09,255
We have got an evolving situation here.

1049
01:04:09,280 --> 01:04:10,931
Did they give you the green light yet?

1050
01:04:11,440 --> 01:04:12,458
They will.

1051
01:04:19,240 --> 01:04:19,969
Owen.

1052
01:04:20,306 --> 01:04:21,633
We have a situation here.

1053
01:04:24,810 --> 01:04:26,010
What he is doing?

1054
01:04:28,920 --> 01:04:30,517
<i>Hey, there. I am Jimmy Fallon.</i>

1055
01:04:30,542 --> 01:04:32,010
<i>Welcome aboard the Gyrosphere,</i>

1056
01:04:32,046 --> 01:04:34,332
<i>an amazing machine
made possible by science.</i>

1057
01:04:34,357 --> 01:04:35,455
<i>Your safety is our main concern.</i>

1058
01:04:35,480 --> 01:04:37,560
<i>Hey, there.
Your safety is our main concern.</i>

1059
01:04:37,606 --> 01:04:39,768
<i>Now just relax and enjoy the ride.</i>

1060
01:05:00,520 --> 01:05:01,773
No, no, no.

1061
01:05:02,173 --> 01:05:02,940
No.

1062
01:05:06,160 --> 01:05:06,933
Hey.

1063
01:05:08,226 --> 01:05:09,273
They made it out.

1064
01:05:22,320 --> 01:05:23,833
Oh, my God, they jumped.

1065
01:05:24,546 --> 01:05:25,547
Brave kids.

1066
01:05:25,680 --> 01:05:26,619
Zach!

1067
01:05:27,236 --> 01:05:28,440
Gray!

1068
01:05:29,420 --> 01:05:31,333
Hey, I am not one of your damn animals.

1069
01:05:31,360 --> 01:05:31,999
Listen.

1070
01:05:32,939 --> 01:05:34,260
Those kids are still alive,

1071
01:05:34,287 --> 01:05:35,962
but you and I will not be...

1072
01:05:36,226 --> 01:05:38,519
if you continue to scream like that.

1073
01:05:39,299 --> 01:05:40,080
So...

1074
01:05:40,880 --> 01:05:42,997
You can pick up their scent, can't you?

1075
01:05:44,137 --> 01:05:45,059
Track their footprints?

1076
01:05:45,084 --> 01:05:46,752
I was with the Navy, not the Navajo.

1077
01:05:46,777 --> 01:05:48,932
So then what should we do?
What do you suggest we do?

1078
01:05:48,957 --> 01:05:50,815
You get back.
I will find them.

1079
01:05:50,840 --> 01:05:52,487
No, we will find them.

1080
01:05:52,905 --> 01:05:54,578
You will last two minutes in there.

1081
01:05:54,699 --> 01:05:56,598
Less, in those ridiculous shoes.

1082
01:06:11,412 --> 01:06:12,669
What is that supposed to mean?

1083
01:06:14,566 --> 01:06:15,729
It means I am ready to go.

1084
01:06:17,253 --> 01:06:18,006
Ok.

1085
01:06:19,366 --> 01:06:21,359
Let's get one thing straight.
I am in charge out here.

1086
01:06:21,384 --> 01:06:23,265
You do everything I say,
exactly as I say it.

1087
01:06:23,290 --> 01:06:24,753
Excuse me?
Just relax.

1088
01:06:27,419 --> 01:06:29,433
It's just like taking
a stroll through the woods.

1089
01:06:31,053 --> 01:06:32,720
65 million years ago.

1090
01:07:08,926 --> 01:07:09,849
Stay here.

1091
01:08:37,646 --> 01:08:38,805
You still have those matches?

1092
01:08:41,320 --> 01:08:42,179
Here you go.

1093
01:09:07,473 --> 01:09:08,080
Gray!

1094
01:09:39,059 --> 01:09:41,290
1992 Jeep Wrangler Sahara.

1095
01:09:41,387 --> 01:09:42,279
Sand Beige.

1096
01:09:45,533 --> 01:09:47,868
You remember when we fixed up
Grandpa's old Malibu, right?

1097
01:09:48,946 --> 01:09:49,788
Yeah.

1098
01:09:58,640 --> 01:10:01,520
Every time this thing kills,
it moves further south.

1099
01:10:01,713 --> 01:10:02,840
It's headed right for the park.

1100
01:10:02,865 --> 01:10:04,166
Why would she come here?

1101
01:10:04,233 --> 01:10:05,997
She can sense thermal radiation.

1102
01:10:06,120 --> 01:10:07,167
Our emergency measures

1103
01:10:07,192 --> 01:10:09,046
just put all the warm bodies in one place.

1104
01:10:11,400 --> 01:10:12,526
Sir...
InGen.

1105
01:10:14,586 --> 01:10:15,626
Hoskins.

1106
01:10:16,809 --> 01:10:18,095
I know who you are.

1107
01:10:18,286 --> 01:10:19,806
Then you know why I am here.

1108
01:10:22,106 --> 01:10:24,766
I have been working for two years
on an application for those Raptors.

1109
01:10:26,806 --> 01:10:28,960
They can hunt and kill that creature.

1110
01:10:29,088 --> 01:10:31,375
But your program
was to test their intelligence.

1111
01:10:31,400 --> 01:10:32,970
Yeah, it was.
And we did.

1112
01:10:33,200 --> 01:10:34,385
And in the process,

1113
01:10:35,126 --> 01:10:36,409
we learned something.

1114
01:10:36,833 --> 01:10:38,177
They follow orders.

1115
01:10:39,337 --> 01:10:41,437
You see, the solution to your crisis

1116
01:10:41,540 --> 01:10:43,144
is standing right in front of you.

1117
01:10:44,359 --> 01:10:46,287
Let me be as clear as I can.

1118
01:10:47,433 --> 01:10:50,994
No Velociraptors are going
to be set loose on this island.

1119
01:10:51,119 --> 01:10:52,166
Oh, shit.

1120
01:10:52,840 --> 01:10:54,365
You are out of your mind!

1121
01:10:54,493 --> 01:10:55,654
What are you going to do
with all these people?

1122
01:10:55,679 --> 01:10:57,759
You got 20,000 people here.
What are you going to do?

1123
01:10:58,060 --> 01:10:59,553
They have no place to go.

1124
01:11:00,327 --> 01:11:01,953
That thing is a killing machine!

1125
01:11:05,013 --> 01:11:06,673
And it will not stop.

1126
01:11:08,400 --> 01:11:09,109
Ok.

1127
01:11:09,739 --> 01:11:11,834
I intend to personally
look into your project,

1128
01:11:11,859 --> 01:11:13,466
to determine its viability,

1129
01:11:14,175 --> 01:11:16,535
within the moral principles
of this company.

1130
01:11:19,339 --> 01:11:20,375
Ok, boss.

1131
01:11:23,000 --> 01:11:24,252
What's your next move?

1132
01:11:33,480 --> 01:11:35,448
Sir, I can't get a hold of your instructor.

1133
01:11:35,680 --> 01:11:36,646
Never mind.

1134
01:11:37,013 --> 01:11:38,853
He is likely caught up in the evacuation.

1135
01:11:38,920 --> 01:11:41,283
You are sure there is nobody else
who can fly a helicopter?

1136
01:11:43,233 --> 01:11:44,570
We don't need anyone else.

1137
01:12:07,466 --> 01:12:08,446
You think it's out there?

1138
01:12:15,102 --> 01:12:16,376
I mean, I know for a fact,

1139
01:12:17,249 --> 01:12:18,489
it is definitely not out there,

1140
01:12:18,736 --> 01:12:19,516
alright?

1141
01:12:19,893 --> 01:12:20,896
We are totally safe.

1142
01:12:21,829 --> 01:12:22,493
Here,

1143
01:12:22,936 --> 01:12:23,909
go take this.

1144
01:12:25,893 --> 01:12:27,102
You are stronger than me.

1145
01:12:38,973 --> 01:12:40,526
Alright. Turn it over.

1146
01:12:44,500 --> 01:12:45,499
It works!

1147
01:12:51,840 --> 01:12:53,366
I thought you failed your driver's test.

1148
01:12:54,059 --> 01:12:55,786
No, only the driving part.

1149
01:13:14,215 --> 01:13:15,408
This one of theirs?

1150
01:13:15,800 --> 01:13:16,593
Yeah.

1151
01:13:18,393 --> 01:13:20,233
That road goes straight back to the park.

1152
01:13:22,800 --> 01:13:25,001
How did they even get
one of these things started?

1153
01:15:09,193 --> 01:15:11,002
Lowery, we found her.

1154
01:15:11,380 --> 01:15:12,841
South of the Gyrosphere Valley,

1155
01:15:12,866 --> 01:15:14,506
between the old park and the Aviary.

1156
01:15:14,724 --> 01:15:16,667
Wait, are you following the dinosaur?

1157
01:15:16,839 --> 01:15:17,375
<i>Yes.</i>

1158
01:15:17,966 --> 01:15:20,179
Get ACU out here.
Real guns this time.

1159
01:15:20,419 --> 01:15:21,874
ACU is airborne.

1160
01:15:21,899 --> 01:15:23,266
<i>They took the helicopter.</i>

1161
01:15:24,053 --> 01:15:25,180
Who is flying it?

1162
01:15:28,086 --> 01:15:30,121
Did you boys serve in the Armed Forces?

1163
01:15:30,266 --> 01:15:31,746
Afghanistan, sir.

1164
01:15:32,400 --> 01:15:34,746
Did your general ever fly
into battle with you?

1165
01:15:38,580 --> 01:15:39,314
Got it!

1166
01:15:40,346 --> 01:15:41,093
Got it.

1167
01:15:42,920 --> 01:15:45,440
<i>We have eyes on the target,
south of the Aviary.</i>

1168
01:15:45,480 --> 01:15:46,509
<i>Proceed and engage.</i>

1169
01:15:46,840 --> 01:15:48,369
Come on! Look alive, boys!

1170
01:15:49,886 --> 01:15:50,696
Look alive!

1171
01:15:59,087 --> 01:16:00,993
10 o'clock!
By the birdcage!

1172
01:16:21,880 --> 01:16:24,451
No, no, no, no, no, no, no, no!

1173
01:16:24,520 --> 01:16:26,526
Looks like the fox got in the henhouse.

1174
01:16:44,520 --> 01:16:46,409
Pull up! Pull up!
Up, up, up!

1175
01:17:20,619 --> 01:17:22,649
We have a breach in the Aviary.

1176
01:17:43,473 --> 01:17:45,286
Trees, the trees!
Go! Go!

1177
01:18:10,580 --> 01:18:11,660
Ok, that's it.

1178
01:18:12,572 --> 01:18:13,654
We are safe now.

1179
01:18:23,393 --> 01:18:24,313
Go, go!

1180
01:18:24,380 --> 01:18:25,950
Go! Go! Go!
Oh, shit!

1181
01:18:27,800 --> 01:18:28,801
Hurry up!

1182
01:18:31,640 --> 01:18:32,606
Hey!

1183
01:18:32,840 --> 01:18:33,841
Help!

1184
01:18:33,920 --> 01:18:35,251
Open the gate!
Let us in!

1185
01:18:35,360 --> 01:18:37,044
Open it up!

1186
01:18:37,120 --> 01:18:38,690
Come on!
Come on!

1187
01:18:38,760 --> 01:18:40,020
That's a first.

1188
01:18:40,639 --> 01:18:42,642
Open the gate!
Open the gate!

1189
01:18:42,667 --> 01:18:43,907
Let us in!

1190
01:18:52,440 --> 01:18:54,635
<i>Attention Aviary employees.</i>

1191
01:18:54,788 --> 01:18:56,629
<i>There has been a containment breach.</i>

1192
01:18:56,940 --> 01:18:57,655
Hello?

1193
01:18:57,913 --> 01:19:00,241
Claire, we spotted
the boys on surveillance.

1194
01:19:00,314 --> 01:19:01,440
They are approaching the west gate.

1195
01:19:01,465 --> 01:19:02,254
I am headed there now.

1196
01:19:02,372 --> 01:19:03,435
Ok. Ok.

1197
01:19:03,892 --> 01:19:04,736
Stay right there.

1198
01:19:05,225 --> 01:19:07,058
I am on my way.
Stay right with them.

1199
01:19:07,320 --> 01:19:08,032
Hey!

1200
01:19:09,126 --> 01:19:10,046
Get on!

1201
01:19:24,255 --> 01:19:25,582
<i>Ladies and gentlemen,</i>

1202
01:19:25,606 --> 01:19:27,243
<i>due to a containment anomaly</i>

1203
01:19:27,268 --> 01:19:29,741
<i>all guests must take
shelter immediately.</i>

1204
01:19:31,393 --> 01:19:32,547
<i>Ladies and gentlemen,</i>

1205
01:19:32,571 --> 01:19:34,220
<i>due to a containment anomaly</i>

1206
01:19:34,260 --> 01:19:36,661
<i>all guests must take shelter immediately.</i>

1207
01:19:39,800 --> 01:19:41,098
<i>Ladies and gentlemen,</i>

1208
01:19:41,122 --> 01:19:42,733
<i>due to a containment anomaly</i>

1209
01:19:42,860 --> 01:19:45,340
<i>all guests must take shelter immediately.</i>

1210
01:20:39,527 --> 01:20:41,447
<i>All units, take position on boardwalk.</i>

1211
01:20:41,559 --> 01:20:42,993
<i>Use liquid tranquilizers.</i>

1212
01:20:43,017 --> 01:20:44,855
<i>Do not fire live ammunition.</i>

1213
01:20:44,880 --> 01:20:45,799
Claire, come on!

1214
01:21:06,500 --> 01:21:07,593
Stop running!

1215
01:21:20,000 --> 01:21:20,560
Wait.

1216
01:21:21,480 --> 01:21:22,660
Don't just stand there!

1217
01:22:03,160 --> 01:22:04,844
Go! Get inside now!

1218
01:22:21,933 --> 01:22:22,847
Zach!

1219
01:22:23,920 --> 01:22:25,046
Gray!

1220
01:22:30,040 --> 01:22:31,591
Aunt Claire!
Go, go!

1221
01:22:31,616 --> 01:22:32,424
Claire!

1222
01:22:34,700 --> 01:22:35,839
No! Hold your...

1223
01:23:01,766 --> 01:23:02,986
Is that Aunt Claire?

1224
01:23:24,000 --> 01:23:24,779
It's them!

1225
01:23:25,136 --> 01:23:25,793
Zach!

1226
01:23:26,880 --> 01:23:27,586
Gray!

1227
01:23:28,240 --> 01:23:29,566
Oh, my God!
Thank God! Thank God!

1228
01:23:29,651 --> 01:23:30,997
What happened? What is this?

1229
01:23:31,251 --> 01:23:32,160
Are you ok?

1230
01:23:32,564 --> 01:23:33,617
Where did you go?

1231
01:23:34,344 --> 01:23:35,985
Why didn't you come back?

1232
01:23:36,757 --> 01:23:38,393
I was so worried about you.
Who is that?

1233
01:23:44,659 --> 01:23:45,820
We work together.

1234
01:23:47,199 --> 01:23:47,968
Hey.

1235
01:23:49,527 --> 01:23:50,415
We gotta go.
Ok.

1236
01:23:50,440 --> 01:23:51,660
Come on, come on.

1237
01:23:54,833 --> 01:23:56,933
Hey, hey. You guys 
can't just be walking up in...

1238
01:23:57,120 --> 01:23:59,873
Simon Masrani's death, was a tragedy.

1239
01:24:01,126 --> 01:24:02,150
The new mission,

1240
01:24:02,693 --> 01:24:03,693
is to prevent...

1241
01:24:03,717 --> 01:24:04,806
further loss of life.

1242
01:24:05,134 --> 01:24:06,245
Who are these guys?

1243
01:24:06,739 --> 01:24:07,861
I am glad you asked.

1244
01:24:08,839 --> 01:24:10,381
You are all relieved of duty.

1245
01:24:11,100 --> 01:24:12,665
There is a new team on the ground.

1246
01:24:32,394 --> 01:24:33,980
Lowery, I am on my way back to you.

1247
01:24:34,022 --> 01:24:35,039
<i>That's a bad idea.</i>

1248
01:24:35,333 --> 01:24:37,200
The board assigned emergency ops

1249
01:24:37,400 --> 01:24:39,022
to iNGen's private security division.

1250
01:24:39,047 --> 01:24:40,620
This guy Hoskins is in charge.

1251
01:24:41,120 --> 01:24:42,720
And he has this insane plan

1252
01:24:42,745 --> 01:24:44,647
to use the Raptors
to hunt the Indominus.

1253
01:24:44,720 --> 01:24:46,688
What do you mean use the Raptors?

1254
01:24:46,880 --> 01:24:48,848
Son of a bitch!

1255
01:24:50,373 --> 01:24:51,565
You should not say bitch.

1256
01:24:51,640 --> 01:24:52,791
Take the kids.

1257
01:24:53,354 --> 01:24:55,093
Get them someplace safe.

1258
01:25:11,240 --> 01:25:13,049
You got this!
Go faster!

1259
01:25:13,074 --> 01:25:14,074
Damn it, drive!

1260
01:25:20,666 --> 01:25:22,184
This does not feel safe.

1261
01:25:22,209 --> 01:25:23,426
Can we stay with you?

1262
01:25:23,520 --> 01:25:25,606
I am never leaving you
as long as you live.

1263
01:25:25,631 --> 01:25:26,597
No, no him.
No.

1264
01:25:29,286 --> 01:25:30,400
Yeah, definitely him.

1265
01:25:58,380 --> 01:25:59,950
<i>Hey! Right here.</i>

1266
01:26:01,646 --> 01:26:02,885
<i>Right here.</i>

1267
01:26:02,960 --> 01:26:04,580
<i>She looks at what she wants.</i>

1268
01:26:06,680 --> 01:26:08,523
Usually what she wants to eat.

1269
01:26:27,827 --> 01:26:29,944
The mother hen has finally arrived.

1270
01:26:33,046 --> 01:26:34,320
Get the hell out of here

1271
01:26:35,100 --> 01:26:36,725
and stay away from my animals.

1272
01:26:37,386 --> 01:26:40,668
Hoskins, you wanted this to happen,
you son of a bitch!

1273
01:26:40,693 --> 01:26:41,958
Oh, Jesus!

1274
01:26:42,711 --> 01:26:44,131
How many more people have to die

1275
01:26:44,384 --> 01:26:46,538
before this mission starts
to make sense to you?

1276
01:26:46,771 --> 01:26:47,816
It's not a mission.

1277
01:26:47,991 --> 01:26:49,081
It's a field test.

1278
01:26:49,847 --> 01:26:52,194
This is an iNGen situation now.

1279
01:26:52,894 --> 01:26:54,762
Ok, there are gonna be cruise ships

1280
01:26:55,001 --> 01:26:56,683
that show up here at first light.

1281
01:26:56,760 --> 01:26:58,240
Everybody is gonna get off this island.

1282
01:26:58,325 --> 01:27:00,035
You are gonna watch a news story
tomorrow?

1283
01:27:00,746 --> 01:27:02,375
About how you all saved lives.

1284
01:27:02,400 --> 01:27:03,500
No, no better yet...

1285
01:27:03,720 --> 01:27:05,926
how your animals saved lives.

1286
01:27:08,746 --> 01:27:10,380
They have never been out of containment.

1287
01:27:10,693 --> 01:27:11,599
It's crazy.

1288
01:27:11,624 --> 01:27:13,504
Let's move it out!
Let's go.

1289
01:27:14,186 --> 01:27:15,310
This is happening!

1290
01:27:16,446 --> 01:27:18,173
With or without you.

1291
01:27:22,686 --> 01:27:24,927
We know that she is in sector five.

1292
01:27:25,120 --> 01:27:27,105
This is a game we call hide-and-seek.

1293
01:27:27,129 --> 01:27:30,126
It's a scent drill we have done it about
a thousand times with these animals.

1294
01:27:30,720 --> 01:27:32,110
When they get on target...

1295
01:27:32,134 --> 01:27:33,993
and they will get on target.

1296
01:27:34,573 --> 01:27:35,980
Wait to engage.

1297
01:27:36,400 --> 01:27:38,526
Velociraptors are pack hunters.

1298
01:27:39,000 --> 01:27:41,484
They like to herd
the animal into a kill zone.

1299
01:27:41,840 --> 01:27:43,130
That's when we take our shot.

1300
01:27:43,160 --> 01:27:44,844
Get a clear shot, wait on my command,

1301
01:27:44,920 --> 01:27:46,570
and give her everything you got.

1302
01:27:46,760 --> 01:27:48,752
We got one good target, gentlemen.

1303
01:27:49,042 --> 01:27:50,575
Do not shoot my Raptors.

1304
01:27:52,040 --> 01:27:52,755
Please.

1305
01:27:53,720 --> 01:27:55,563
Easy, Blue.

1306
01:27:56,680 --> 01:27:57,986
Easy.

1307
01:27:59,480 --> 01:28:00,720
Attagirl.

1308
01:28:03,440 --> 01:28:04,860
You don't scare me.

1309
01:28:05,406 --> 01:28:06,306
Owen.

1310
01:28:11,479 --> 01:28:12,385
Are they safe?

1311
01:28:13,920 --> 01:28:14,921
No, they are not.

1312
01:28:15,880 --> 01:28:16,972
What are their names?

1313
01:28:17,840 --> 01:28:18,531
Well,

1314
01:28:18,772 --> 01:28:19,601
you got Charlie.

1315
01:28:19,920 --> 01:28:20,773
There is Echo.

1316
01:28:21,224 --> 01:28:22,225
Here is Delta.

1317
01:28:22,840 --> 01:28:24,037
This one is called Blue.

1318
01:28:25,278 --> 01:28:26,272
She is the beta.

1319
01:28:26,740 --> 01:28:27,821
Who is the alpha?

1320
01:28:28,240 --> 01:28:29,539
You are looking at him, kid.

1321
01:28:35,080 --> 01:28:35,882
See?

1322
01:28:36,287 --> 01:28:37,115
Totally safe.

1323
01:28:38,880 --> 01:28:39,928
Alright, get in.

1324
01:28:40,125 --> 01:28:40,889
Come on.

1325
01:28:41,307 --> 01:28:42,195
Get in there.

1326
01:28:44,886 --> 01:28:45,892
If you need me,

1327
01:28:46,406 --> 01:28:47,615
I will be right up front.

1328
01:28:47,840 --> 01:28:49,493
Just open that window.

1329
01:28:50,180 --> 01:28:51,001
Ok?

1330
01:28:52,186 --> 01:28:53,312
Put your seatbelts on.

1331
01:28:57,080 --> 01:28:58,486
Ok, so just...

1332
01:29:00,259 --> 01:29:01,162
Hold hands.

1333
01:29:21,090 --> 01:29:22,450
Nothing is getting in here, right?

1334
01:29:26,320 --> 01:29:27,008
Hey.

1335
01:29:29,661 --> 01:29:30,687
Do you remember that ghost,

1336
01:29:31,037 --> 01:29:32,397
at the old house?
Remember, the...

1337
01:29:32,881 --> 01:29:34,094
